man and Captain Caine but they are soon joined by Ford, Ryder and Gregor. In a twist of fate, Ford is double crossed by the Organization and Lok chooses to save him."},{"heading":"Gallery","level":2,"wikitext":"<gallery>\nFile:The Lost City of Casterwill cover.jpg|Full cover artwork\n</gallery>\n[[Category:Comics| 12]]{{Clear}}{{ComicsNav}}","text":"File:The Lost City of Casterwill cover.jpg|Full cover artwork"}],"full_text":"The Lost City of Casterwill is the 12th issue of the Huntik Magazine comic book series and the final issue in the first series of comics.\n\n== Synopsis ==\nIn the underwater city of Ys, the Huntik team battle Dr. Rickman and Captain Caine but they are soon joined by Ford, Ryder and Gregor. In a twist of fate, Ford is double crossed by the Organization and Lok chooses to save him.\n\n== Gallery ==\n\nFile:The Lost City of Casterwill cover.jpg|Full cover artwork","raw_wikitext":"{{stub}}\n{{Infobox comic\n| image      = File:HM12 Lost City of Casterwill Cover.jpeg\n| issue      = 12\n| released       = September 2010\n| previous   = [[The Seekers of Ys]]\n| italian    = La città perduta dei Casterwill\n| writer            = [[Sean Molyneaux]]\n| director          = [[Simone Borselli]]\n| locations = [[Ys]]\n| next       = [[The Secret of the Flying Dutchman]]\n| new titans = [[Geisha]]<br>[[Land Shark]]<br>[[Red Vampress]]\n}}\n'''The Lost City of Casterwill''' is the 12th issue of the ''[[Huntik Magazine]]'' comic book series and the final issue in the first series of comics.\n\n== Synopsis ==\nIn the underwater city of [[Ys]], the Huntik team battle [[Dr. Rickman]] and [[Captain Caine]] but they are soon joined by [[Ford]], [[Ryder]] and [[Gregor]]. In a twist of fate, Ford is double crossed by [[the Organization]] and [[Lok]] chooses to save him.\n\n== Gallery ==\n<gallery>\nFile:The Lost City of Casterwill cover.jpg|Full cover artwork\n</gallery>\n[[Category:Comics| 12]]{{Clear}}{{ComicsNav}}","categories":["Article stubs","Comics"],"links":